    "q-119185": {
      "dom_id": "step-q119185",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "An oil tank has a leak. The rate of change of the volume $V$ (in liters) of oil in the tank is directly proportional to the time $t$ (in minutes) passed since the tank started leaking. However, the tank is also refilled with $4$ liters of oil every minute. What is the differential equation that describes the rate of change of the volume of oil in the tank at time $t?$",
      "worked_solution": "The rate of change in the oil volume decreases in proportion to time $t$ and increases by $4$ liters per minute. The differential equation that describes this is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t}=-kt+4,\n$$\n\nwhere $k$ is the (positive) constant of proportionality.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
