    "q-79310": {
      "dom_id": "step-q79310",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "A cyclist has a small puncture in one of her tires. The volume of air $V,$ in centimeters cubed, in the tire decreases at a rate that's proportional to the volume at that moment. Every day, the cyclist pumps $10\\,{\\text{cm}}^{3}$ back into the tire.\nWhat is the differential equation describing the rate of change of the volume of air in the tire  at time $t,$ where $t$ is the time in days?",
      "worked_solution": "The rate of change in the volume of air per day decreases in proportion to $V$ and increases by $12.$ The differential equation that describes this is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t}=-kV+10,\n$$\n\nwhere $k$ is the (positive) constant of proportionality.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
